            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> why? other modules set their own filetypes. for consistency's sake, so should clue\n\nThat's not enough motivation. Not all buffers need a filetype and not all scratch buffers in 'mini.nvim' have a filetype. There are no plans to make the 'mini.clue' buffer itself adjustable by users and I don't see a uses case for when having a filetype is needed. There is currently a way to identify a 'mini.clue' buffer by using its name, as the naming scheme *is* documented as a general principle.\n\n---\n\nPlease follow the templates for opening a new issue/PR/discussion. This is not the first time you do not follow them. The next time this happens I'll be very inclined to close the issue/PR/discussion immediately.",
